/* book: lead: A loop much smaller than a wavelength carries nearly the same current all the way round, so it behaves as a magnetic dipole: the short dipole’s doughnut pattern with E and H exchanged. Its radiation resistance grows as the fourth power of its size, so it radiates poorly; as a receiver that hardly matters, which is why a coil on a ferrite rod sits in every AM radio. */
