/* book Worked example: Q: A small loop has N = 10 turns of radius a = 0.1 m and works at 10 MHz. Its loss resistance is 0.05 Ω. Check that it is small, and find its radiation resistance and radiation efficiency.
   1. λ = c/f = 3 × 10⁸ / 10⁷ = 30 m.
   2. C = 2π × 0.1 = 0.628 m and λ/10 = 3 m, so C < λ/10: the loop is small.
   3. A = πa² = π × 0.01 = 0.0314 m², so NA/λ² = 10 × 0.0314/900 = 3.49 × 10⁻⁴.
   4. Rr = 31 171 × (3.49 × 10⁻⁴)² = 31 171 × 1.218 × 10⁻⁷ = 3.80 × 10⁻³ Ω = 3.8 mΩ.
   5. ηrad = Rr/(Rr + RL) = 0.0038/0.0538 = 0.071, about 7 per cent.
   Answer: The loop is small (0.628 m < 3 m); Rr = 3.8 mΩ; ηrad ≈ 7 per cent. */
